Subject: [PATCH 13/13] jm-v7 013: Bifrost BC emulation: decode
 zero-initialized images on JM

textureCompressionBC is already advertised on v6/v7: the BC emulation
(csf-v11 022/039/040/108) is arch-independent. panvk_bc_emul_enabled()
does not look at the arch, a BC image is LINEAR with a decoded plane
after the raw blocks, uploads and copies decode through the compute
shaders in panvk_vX_cmd_meta.c, and views sample the decoded plane. The
fragment decode into compact shadows (150, 180, 185) is v10+ only
(image->bc_gfx), so Bifrost always takes the compute path, as v9 does.

The one missing piece on JM was the decode of images leaving
VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_ZERO_INITIALIZED_EXT (040): only the CSF barrier called
cmd_bc_decode_zero_initialized(), so on v6/v7 such an image sampled the
zeroed decoded plane instead of the decode of zero blocks (opaque black
for BC1). The JM barrier now calls it on v6/v7. v9 JM has the same gap and
is left unchanged here.

Build-tested only, no Bifrost device run. biblioklept

